            <div xml:id="d84">

                <pb facs="0179" n="59" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg59"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/3058</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-06">May 6, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received May 8.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 680</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    President yesterday signed decrees restoring the suspended constitutional
                    guarantees in the provinces of Santa Clara and Camaguey.</p>
                <pb facs="0180" n="60" xml:id="pg60"/>
                <p>Constitutional guarantees thus remain suspended only in the province of Habana,
                    as they were restored in Oriente, Pinar del Rio and Matanzas on April 20.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward L. Reed</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
